```json
"Condition": {
  "StringEquals": { "iam:PassedToService": "textract.amazonaws.com" }
}
```

because the role was originally set up for Textract. That condition is satisfied when Textract calls `AssumeRole`, but it fails the moment Comprehend tries to assume the same role — producing `AccessDeniedException` on the `StartEntitiesDetectionJob` call. The Comprehend action permission looks fine (and is), which is exactly why this one gets missed.

